      "content": "I'll read the original test file first to understand what needs to be improved.Now I'll write the improved version with better understandability — removing unused fields/helpers, adding a clear test-purpose comment, and naming the intermediate variables descriptively.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes 13 unused instance fields and 3 unused helper methods that cluttered the single-test class, renames `x` to `emptyData` and the intermediate variance variable to `expectedVariance` for clarity, aligns the assertions vertically so the `stats.getXxx()` calls are visually grouped, and adds a class-level Javadoc and a brief inline comment explaining the test's intent — all without changing any called methods, arguments, or expected outcomes."
